# SQL files are checksummed byte-for-byte:
#   - Prisma stores a SHA-256 of each migration.sql in _prisma_migrations
#   - backend/prisma/repair/manifest.json stores one per repair file
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows dev machines, so without this rule a
# fresh checkout would rewrite these files to CRLF. That changes their bytes,
# which changes every hash, which would make the migration runner report each
# applied migration as a checksum mismatch and the repair registry refuse to
# run all 17 repairs — on files that are in fact untouched and correct.
#
# Pin them to LF on every platform.
*.sql text eol=lf
backend/prisma/repair/manifest.json text eol=lf
